hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15806","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: al-Zubaydi narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that there was no storytelling in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor of Abu Bakr, and the first who told stories was Tamim al-Dari; he asked permission of Umar ibn al-Khattab to tell stories to the people standing, and Umar gave him permission."
"15807","Yaqub narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Ubaydillah al-Zuhri narrated to me, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, nephew of Namir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had only one muadhdhin for all the prayers, for Friday and others, who would call the adhan and the iqamah. He said: Bilal would call the adhan when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sat on the minbar on Friday, and would call the iqamah when he came down, and likewise for Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, until it was Uthman."
"15808","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah said, and I heard it myself from Harun, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Aswad al-Qurashi narrated to us that Yazid ibn Khusayfah narrated to him, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My nation will remain upon the natural disposition as long as they pray Maghrib before the rising of the stars."
"15809","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Yusuf, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, he said: I was taken for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the Farewell Pilgrimage, when I was seven years old."
"15810","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Juayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, he said: A drinker would be brought in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and during the rule of Abu Bakr and the early part of the rule of Umar, and we would stand to him and strike him with our hands and our sandals and our cloaks, until it was the early part of the rule of Umar and he flogged forty for it, then when they exceeded in it and transgressed he flogged eighty."
"15811","Makki narrated to us: al-Juayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O Aishah, do you know this woman? She said: No, O Prophet of Allah. He said: This is the singing girl of the sons of so-and-so; would you like her to sing for you? She said: Yes. He said: So he gave her a dish and she sang for her, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Satan has blown into her nostrils."
"15812","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, he said: I went out with the boys to Thaniyyat al-Wada to meet the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the expedition of Tabuk. And Sufyan once said: I remember the arrival of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived from Tabuk."
"15813","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Khusayfah narrated to us, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, if Allah wills, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wore two coats of mail one over the other on the day of Uhud. And he narrated it to us another time and did not make the exception in it."
"15814","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Idris and Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, nephew of Namir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had only one muadhdhin who would call the adhan when he sat on the minbar and would call the iqamah when he came down, and Abu Bakr likewise and Umar likewise, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both."
"15815","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that Shurayh al-Hadrami was mentioned, he said: He was mentioned before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: That is a man who does not take the Quran as a pillow."
"15816","SOURCE TRUNCATED: Narrated to us."
"15817","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: al-Saib ibn Yazid informed me, and he mentioned the like of it."
"15818","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: al-Saib ibn Yazid, nephew of Namir, narrated to me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No contagion, no Safar, and no Hamah."
"15819","Waki narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, he said: The adhan in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both, was two adhans, until it was the time of Uthman and the people increased, so he ordered the first adhan at al-Zawra."
"15820","Yunus narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Jafar, he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no person who is in a gathering and then says when he wants to rise: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You, except that he is forgiven for what was in that gathering. So I narrated this hadith to Yazid ibn Khusayfah, and he said: Thus al-Saib ibn Yazid narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
